# DTF tier manifest: npm-anon-audit  (artifact-keeper#4317, fixed by #4785, 1.11.3)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + the real npm CLI client (client.npm). The
# bug lives in repo_visibility_middleware, ahead of any storage backend, so the
# storage dimension is irrelevant.
#
# THE BUG (#4317)
# `npm audit` (and the audit step of `npm install`) POSTs the dependency tree to
#     /npm/<repo>/-/npm/v1/security/advisories/bulk   (npm >= 7)
#     /npm/<repo>/-/npm/v1/security/audits/quick      (npm 6, yarn, fallback)
# repo_visibility_middleware treats every anonymous POST as a write (#508) and
# answered 401, so an anonymous client of a PUBLIC npm repository got "Unable
# to authenticate". The permission arm also classified the POST as a write, so
# an authenticated non-admin without write got 403. The fix (#4785) adds exactly
# those two routes to both read-classified POST allowlists
# (is_anonymous_readable_format_post and is_non_mutating_format_post).
# Repository visibility is unchanged: a private repo still refuses anonymous.
#
# THE 1.12.0 CONTRACT CHANGE (#5631, fixed by #5778)
# Below 1.12.0 a hosted repo, and a Remote whose upstream is unreachable,
# answered the audit routes with an empty report (200 {}), which npm prints as
# "found 0 vulnerabilities": a false clean result. From 1.12.0 a hosted repo
# answers 501 {"error":"npm audit is not available through repository ..."}
# and an unreachable Remote answers 503 {"error":"npm audit could not be
# performed ..."}. The oracle reads the backend version from /health and
# asserts the contract of that version; #4317 is about the route not REFUSING
# the caller, so the honest 501/503 is a pass there and 401/403 is a fail.
#
# Oracle (oracle.sh, RELEASE_GATE=1):
#   (FIX #4317) RED on 1.11.2: anonymous bulk + quick on a public hosted npm
#             repo and on a public remote npm repo are not refused; a non-admin
#             user with no write is not refused on the public repo nor, with a
#             read grant, on a private repo. "Not refused" is 200 + npm JSON
#             below 1.12.0 and 501 (hosted) / 503 (remote, no egress) with the
#             JSON error above from 1.12.0. Below 1.12.0 a real anonymous
#             `npm audit` against the public repo exits 0.
#   (FIX #5631) from 1.12.0: a real anonymous `npm audit` against the public
#             hosted repo exits non-zero with "not available through
#             repository", never "found 0 vulnerabilities" and never an auth
#             refusal.
#   (CONTROL) true on every image: anonymous bulk + quick on a PRIVATE npm
#             repo are refused (401, the unauthenticated challenge); admin bulk
#             + quick are not refused on public and private (same per-version
#             answer as above); anonymous publish (PUT) and an anonymous POST
#             one segment past the audit route stay 401; the real anonymous
#             `npm install` from the public repo succeeds.
#
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS stays at the base default (false): the remote
# repo's upstream is an unresolvable `.invalid` host, so its audit falls back
# to the empty report (< 1.12.0) or answers 503 (>= 1.12.0); nothing is ever
# fetched.
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~40 calls incl. Basic-auth bcrypt; keep parity with
# the other API tiers so a re-run under load never throttles a probe into a 429.
COVERS="4317 5631"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem client.npm"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
